author: codex
estimated_minutes: 480
acceptance_criteria: "Maintainer approves the destructive history-rewrite and identity mapping plan; Every reachable ref is rewritten or retired so the filename-only host-path scan returns zero; Commit authors use the approved public noreply identity throughout rewritten history; Secret scanning, PM history verification, clone acceptance, tags, open PRs, and downstream coordination are revalidated after the rewrite; No npm release is published before the rewritten remote and local canonical checkout agree"
blocked_reason: "Requires explicit maintainer approval for destructive public history rewrite, tag migration, and force-update coordination."
severity: critical
environment: "All refs in the public pm-csv repository, 195 commits as of 2026-08-20"
repro_steps: Enumerate git rev-list --all; scan blobs by filename for absolute home paths; count git log author emails.
expected_result: "All reachable public history contains no private host paths, personal email identities, secrets, or keys, with a documented canonical identity mapping."
actual_result: 283 host-path blob hits remain and 106 commits use a personal email; zero high-confidence secret token/private-key hits.
